category: science

entry matter
term: Matter
related_terms: atom
related_terms: element
related_terms: proton
quick_facts: Matter has mass and takes up space
quick_facts: Solids, liquids and gases are all matter
quick_facts: Air is matter: a pumped-up ball weighs more than a flat one
quick_facts: Light and heat are energy, not matter
quick_facts: All matter is made of atoms

sources:
    {"organization":"OpenStax","title":"Chemistry 2e: Phases and Classification of Matter","url":"https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/1-2-phases-and-classification-of-matter"}

definition:
    Anything that has mass and takes up space. Solids, liquids and gases are all matter, and so is air. All matter is made of atoms. Light and heat are not matter: they are forms of energy. Sound is not matter either, but a wave that travels through matter.

debunking_snippet:
    “Air is nothing.” Air is matter. It is made of atoms joined in tiny groups, it has mass, and it takes up space.
